<h1>TImageButton</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TImageButton" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TImageButton</tt> extends <a href="?page=Controls.Image">TImage</a> and posts back
when the user clicks the image. It renders an <tt>&lt;input type="image"&gt;</tt> element.
<tt>ImageUrl</tt> names the image, and <tt>Text</tt> sets its alternate text.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TImageButton ImageUrl="search.png" Text="Search" OnClick="runSearch" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>The click coordinate</h2>

<p class="block-content">
A browser posts the point inside the image where the click landed. The control passes it
to the <tt>OnClick</tt> handler as a <tt>TImageClickEventParameter</tt>, which carries
<tt>X</tt> and <tt>Y</tt> in pixels measured from the top left corner of the image. The
<tt>OnCommand</tt> event carries a command parameter instead, so a handler that needs the
coordinate uses <tt>OnClick</tt>.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
public function runSearch($sender, $param)
{
    $this-&gt;Result-&gt;Text = "You clicked at {$param-&gt;X}, {$param-&gt;Y}.";
}
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>Shared behavior</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The control raises <tt>OnClick</tt> and <tt>OnCommand</tt>, honors <tt>CommandName</tt>
and <tt>CommandParameter</tt>, triggers validation through <tt>CausesValidation</tt> and
<tt>ValidationGroup</tt>, and answers the return key when <tt>IsDefaultButton</tt> is
true. It inherits <tt>ImageAlign</tt> and <tt>DescriptionUrl</tt> from <tt>TImage</tt>,
and both are deprecated for the reasons given on that page. An image map that responds
differently to different regions of one image is
<a href="?page=Controls.ImageMap">TImageMap</a>.
</p>
